*Summary*
In this file, the weights for inverse probability weighting are generated. We use the same variables as used in Feng, 2021, plus trial arm, in a logistic regression model for the probability of an antibody sample being taken. 
One model is run for the neutralising Ab measure, and one for both the spike and RBD binding Ab measure, because the latter two had the same missing data.

# 1. Setup

```{r setup, include=FALSE}
knitr::opts_chunk$set(echo = TRUE)
library(ResourceSelection)
insertRow <- function(existingDF, newrow, r) {
  existingDF[seq(r+1,nrow(existingDF)+1),] <- existingDF[seq(r,nrow(existingDF)),]
  existingDF[r,] <- newrow
  existingDF
}
```



